 "roles": {
  "_note": "Each role: family, name, 'requires' (any one of the listed alternatives; each alternative is {signal: minimum}, and a signal must be above its minimum), and 'weights'. A weight key can be a group: 'a|b' reads the best of them (any one will do), 'a&b' the weakest (it needs both). The fit is the weighted mean of the signals over the positive weights, clipped to 0-1; negative weights pull it down. A role whose gate isn't met scores 0 and says what it needs. 'prior' (default 1) discounts the broad, stat-shaped roles a little, so that a role defined by a specific move, item or ability wins a tie. 'ev_template' only steers where the solver starts; the score alone decides.",

  "physical_setup_sweeper": {"family": "offense", "name": "physical setup sweeper",
